Negative control for the form's BOOT being drawn in the shape of what is coming
(`C8`) — the manage-dialog skeleton-boot spec.

A form that has not presented yet draws its OWN frame: a label and a control per
field, under the action bar's own placement, so nothing moves when the real
controls land. The mutant puts the notice back in front of it and stops the
notice standing aside while the module is loading — the exact pair that had a
forced `loading` on a form drawing a blue "one moment" panel where the form was
about to be. Nothing else moves: the skeleton is still built, still counted off
the uischema, and still rendered once the notice is out of the way.

What must go red is the PICTURE a booting form draws, not the presence of a
loading state. An assertion that only reads `isLoading`, or that counts
`Skeleton` components without asserting no notice stands in their place, passes
the mutant unchanged.

Re-armed 2026-09-12: the skeleton branch moved ahead of the notice when forced
loading was fixed, so the mutant now restores BOTH halves of the old order.
Re-armed again the same day: `notice` gained a forced-read-failure branch, so
the hunk that strips its loading guard now sits under that branch.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the manage-dialog skeleton-boot spec — a booting editor draws field
placeholders, never a notice.

